A||||3||MooCow||How do I do the headlight code thing?||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||09-14-2000||01:47 PM||||Okay How do I make my car read out all of teh codes with its headlight??  I think this can be done because I got all of the codes on a piece of paper but do not know how to set teh codes of to see if my car has anything wrong with it.  Anyone know how to do this?  Is it hard to do?<P>                             Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-14-2000||02:03 PM||||The Check Engine light is what will flash the codes.  It's pretty easy to do, just remove the black panel that covers the cigarette lighter in the center console.  Look in the Tips at the bottom part of <A HREF="http://www.lookinhere.com/automobiles/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>Bill Gorman's Fiero Tips & Links</A> for the instructions.  Pretty sure his info is correct.  Hayne's manual has the instructions too, but I don't have that on hand where I'm at now.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">    <BR>    <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||09-14-2000||02:14 PM||||MooCow, its not in the headlights, its in the CHECK ENGINE light. What you do is ground out the first two ports in the connection under the lighter cover.<P>Take off the lighter cover (two screws).<BR>Turn ignition to ON, do not start the car though. <BR>There are two rows of ports. On the left side (passenger side of car), ground out the two top ports closest to the left. I uses a paperclip to ground them together. one tip in one side, one tip in the other side. <P>Auto Zone gives away GM keys. I now have one, its alot easier to put a key in, instead of bending a paperclip to fit. <P>Let  me know if i missed something fella's.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||10
Z||000003||JohnnyK||09-14-2000||11:42 PM||||Yeah, the passenger side of the car is right side of the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
